pansion of electrical infrastructure. Invented by notable figures such as Thomas Edison and subsequently refined by others, the meter became crucial for the burgeoning electric utility industry, facilitating the commercialization of electricity across Europe and North America. By the early 20th century, electricity meters were widely installed in homes and businesses, changing how energy was consumed and billed.

